Spec: Project/Modules

Purpose:
  Declare each concrete module in the SDDRA ecosystem — what it owns,
  its public API surface, and its direct dependencies. Modules are the
  deployable/code-boundary units that implement domains.

Rules:
  A module MUST declare what it owns.
  A module MUST declare its public API surface.
  A module MUST explicitly declare its dependencies (`deps`).
  A module MUST NOT depend on any module not listed in its declared deps.
  A module MAY declare `files` (owned source paths) — routing pointers only.
  A module MAY declare `tests` (owned test paths) — routing pointers only.
  A module MAY declare `bounded_contexts` when a domain spans multiple implementations.

Note:
  This file contains CONCRETE module declarations for the SDDRA ecosystem.
  Each module maps to a real codebase under ./tmp/.

Modules:

  captainup-gamification:
    purpose: CaptainUp gamification platform integration — points, badges, leaderboards, player profiles
    domain: Integration + Notification + EventProcessing + Scheduling + Gamification
    path: (external platform — no local codebase)
    bounded_contexts:
      - gamification-rules (rule engine for points, badges, achievements)
      - gamification-leaderboard (ranked lists, scopes, caching)
      - gamification-player (player profile, auid mapping, progression)
      - gamification-anticheat (validation, anomaly detection, rollback)
    owns:
      - Event ingestion (WebSocket firehose, async queue)
      - Rule evaluation engine (declarative, async, idempotent)
      - Point award processing (idempotent, auditable)
      - Badge unlock evaluation (time-window, streak, dependencies)
      - Leaderboard write/read models (CQRS, sorted sets, snapshots)
      - Player profile sync (async, bidirectional mapping)
      - Anti-cheat detection (async, rate limiting, anomaly detection)
      - CaptainUp HTTP and WebSocket clients
      - Scheduled sync jobs (leaderboard rebuild, badge evaluation, profile sync)
      - Mailgun/Slack notification providers for gamification events
    api:
      - evaluateRules(event, userState) -> {actions}
      - getLeaderboard(scope, page) -> {entries}
      - getUserRank(userId, scope) -> {rank, score}
      - getPlayerProfile(userId) -> PlayerProfile
      - syncPlayerProfile(userId) -> void
      - awardPoints(userId, amount, reason) -> PointEvent
      - unlockBadge(userId, badgeId) -> BadgeEvent
      - processAction(userId, actionType, context) -> void
    deps:
      - supabase (database + RPC functions)
      - captainup (external gamification API)
      - mailgun (email provider)
      - slack (notification webhook)
      - redis (cache, sorted sets, rate limits)
    files:
      - (module boundary defined by bounded contexts above)
    tests:
      - (tests defined per bounded context)
    state: active

  pultapaz:
    purpose: Bank and MFO credit integration platform with quiz-based routing
    domain: Integration + User + Notification + Scheduling
    path: ./tmp/pultapaz
    bounded_contexts:
      - integration-execution (HTTP calls to bank/MFO APIs)
      - pre-check-validation (identity verification before submission)
      - status-polling (application status tracking)
      - mail-integration (async email via RabbitMQ)
      - batch-pre-check (multi-integration batch validation)
      - condition-evaluation (dynamic routing rules)
    owns:
      - IntegrationService (HTTP execution, retry, response mapping)
      - MailIntegrationService (template rendering, daily limits)
      - BatchPreCheckService (batch identity validation)
      - IntegrationConditionService (dynamic routing rules)
      - RabbitMQ consumers (mail, batch, realtime)
      - IntegrationField model (request/response mapping, transforms)
      - IntegrationCondition model (amount, duration, employment rules)
      - Delayed task commands (add, add_batch, execute)
      - SMS and Telegram notification providers
    api:
      - processIntegration(quizParams, redirectId, alias) -> {results}
      - executePreCheck(integration, values) -> {passed, message}
      - checkApplicationStatus(integration, externalId, redirectId) -> {status, code}
      - processWebhookResponse(integrationName, data) -> {mapped_fields}
      - evaluateConditions(integrationId, redirect, params) -> {passed}
      - sendIntegrationMail(integration, quizParams, redirectId) -> {success}
    deps:
      - mysql (primary database)
      - redis (cache, session, queue)
      - rabbitmq (async message processing)
      - guzzle (HTTP client for external APIs)
    files:
      - backend/**/*
      - api/**/*
      - common/**/*
      - console/**/*
      - frontend/**/*
      - src/integration/**/*
      - src/consumer/**/*
      - src/event/**/*
      - src/delayed_task/**/*
      - src/sms/**/*
      - src/telegram/**/*
      - src/salesdoubler/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/**/*
    state: active

  rovio-matchmaking:
    purpose: Multi-game queue and matchmaking microservice
    domain: Integration (game infrastructure) + EventProcessing
    path: ./tmp/Rovio.Matchmaking
    bounded_contexts:
      - queue-management (enqueue, cancel, poll)
      - session-formation (match creation, late join)
      - game-config (durable config in Postgres, hot projection to Redis)
    owns:
      - QueueService (ticket enqueue, cancel, poll)
      - SessionService (session formation, late join)
      - GameConfigService (CRUD, Redis projection)
      - MatchmakingEngine (ticket selection, session formation)
      - MatchingService (latency + wait-time compatibility)
      - Redis adapters (ticket store, session store, shard lock, config runtime)
      - Postgres repository (game match config)
    api:
      - enqueue(gameId, playerId, region, latencyMs) -> TicketDto
      - getTicket(gameId, ticketId) -> TicketDto
      - cancelTicket(gameId, ticketId) -> void
      - getSession(sessionId) -> SessionDto
      - lateJoin(sessionId, playerId, region, latencyMs) -> SessionDto
      - upsertGameConfig(gameId, config) -> GameMatchConfigDto
      - getGameConfig(gameId) -> GameMatchConfigDto
    deps:
      - postgres (durable game config)
      - redis (queues, tickets, sessions, locks, projected config)
      - efcore (ORM for Postgres)
    files:
      - src/Rovio.Domain.Common/**/*
      - src/Rovio.Matchmaking.Domain/**/*
      - src/Rovio.Matchmaking.Application/**/*
      - src/Rovio.Matchmaking.Infrastructure/**/*
      - src/Rovio.Matchmaking.Api/**/*
      - src/Rovio.Matchmaking.Worker/**/*
    tests:
      - tests/Rovio.Domain.Common.Tests.Unit/**/*
      - tests/Rovio.Matchmaking.Domain.Tests.Unit/**/*
      - tests/Rovio.Matchmaking.Application.Tests.Unit/**/*
      - tests/Rovio.Matchmaking.Infrastructure.Tests.Integration/**/*
      - tests/Rovio.Matchmaking.Api.Tests.Integration/**/*
    state: active

Rules:
  [M1] A module MUST declare all direct dependencies.
  [M2] A module MUST NOT depend on another module's internal structures.
  [M3] A module's public API is its contract — internal implementation may change.
  [M4] A module MAY implement multiple bounded contexts from one or more domains.
  [M5] A module's `files` and `tests` declarations are routing pointers, not source of truth.
  [M6] A module MUST be independently testable.
  [M7] A module SHOULD be independently deployable when service extraction is needed.
  [M8] Module boundaries MUST align with domain boundaries.

Navigation:
  Domains: @domains.sdd
  Flows: @flows.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/principles.sdd

State: +
